          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "In this section, we prove that the Möbius energy of a knot is bounded by the ropelength. Our goal is partly the theorem itself and partly the paradigm: any “energy” deﬁned in terms of inverse-square distances should have an analogous bound, with the proof following this model. Theorem 8. If K is a smooth knot in R3 then EO4(K) < 4.57EL(K)4/3. (3) Theorem 9. If K is a smooth knot in R3 then EO4(K) ⩽1 4EL(K)2. (4)",
      "extractCut": true
    },
